            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> We pretty much own it now.\r\n\r\nThat's very good to know, and I'll keep it in mind! But I'm somewhat interested in upstreaming some of my changes regardless at some point, even if they don't apply cleanly.\r\n\r\n> It might be worth upstreaming this change there first\r\n\r\nI have several reasons to start with Neovim, for example: I use it a lot more, and the status line DSL seems more important to Neovim, since it's using it for its own default features, which also makes it easier for me to argue for my changes. But I can also think of a lot of reasons to start upstream. Do you have a specific reason in mind? Does it maybe make synchronisation between the projects easier because there's a process in that direction? Or is it to get more review, or to reduce chance of divergence?",
