            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Do you have a specific reason in mind?\r\n\r\nJust as a general policy if we’re changing code that is shared with Vim we try to get it in Vim first and then merge the upstream patch. Both for maintenance reasons (it makes merging future patches easier if the code is similar) and general project synergy.\r\n\r\nBut as Justin pointed out it’s a moot point in this case. If you want to adapt and upstream your changes to Vim too that’s fine of course but we wouldn’t use that patch ourselves, so it’s not relevant to this PR. ",
